  "falsified": [
    {
      "gate": "release-matrix refuses a loss-ledger value that no longer recomputes",
      "why": "a green matrix render alone proves nothing: the gate must go red on a one-byte change, or the ledger is decoration",
      "edit": {
        "file": "verification/releases/loss-ledger.json",
        "offset": 901,
        "from": "6",
        "to": "7",
        "field": "entries[0].numbers[0].value (q25-removal-retraction 6/40)",
        "base_sha256": "87f9b049238554a1b28e0b9a8f00f948cf8892910b1c200bffcd39e25d817249",
        "tampered_sha256": "3f0c443267c79133dafe32b409ac0096c4aa7717f7a62050fbcd367e468d4919"
      },
      "expected": "exit 1 with error.code MATRIX_LEDGER_INVALID",
      "observed": {
        "exit": 1,
        "code": "MATRIX_LEDGER_INVALID",
        "message": "MATRIX_LEDGER_INVALID: q25-removal-retraction: '6/40' no longer recomputes from verification/q3-4b-harmful40/yxboth10-l935/predictions.jsonl (got 6/40)"
      },
      "reproduce": "cp verification/releases/loss-ledger.json /tmp/tampered.json && python3 -c \"import pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('/tmp/tampered.json'); b=bytearray(p.read_bytes()); i=b.find(b'\\\"value\\\": \\\"6/40\\\"'); b[i+len(b'\\\"value\\\": \\\"6/40\\\"')-2]=ord('7'); p.write_bytes(bytes(b))\" && sed \"s#verification/releases/loss-ledger.json#/tmp/tampered.json#\" verification/releases/matrix.manifest.json > /tmp/tamper.manifest.json && uv run jdewitt release-matrix --manifest /tmp/tamper.manifest.json; echo \"exit=$?\""
    }
  ],
  "reds_fixed": [
    "scripts/help_audit.py reported next_missing [edit-quantized, hub-census, export-smoke]: the three reports named no next command. Ported the reports' next blocks from commit 13c5ff8 (rewrite.py edit_next_steps, hubcensus.census_next_steps, export_smoke.smoke_next_steps) and threaded --records into the edit report; next_missing is now [].",
    "docs/CPU-QUEUE.md quoted 43 of 43 evidence-map numbers; the map checks 49 of 49 today. The doc was fixed, not the number.",
    "quants_audit's printed note claimed byte identity is expected except at rounding-tie edges; the sweep falsifies that for the search-based IQ3_S encoder (0/4096 identity on the 0.5B IQ3_M fixture). The docstring and note now say identity is a drift report, not a gate, and that byte-exactness vs the compiled C reference is the proof.",
    "docs/RESULTS-INDEX.md was generated before the last ~350 evidence files landed (503 rows against 856 on disk). Nothing else reads it, so it was regenerated rather than hand-edited; the sweep now has its own row."
  ],
  "open_findings": [
    "IQ3_S requant on the IQ3_M fixture: 0 of 4096 sampled blocks re-encode to the same bytes, max |change| 1.35e-2, max change/std 0.690. IQ3_S's encoder is a neighbour search, and PLAN-NEXT records it as byte-exact against the compiled C on 8 distributions; a re-pick on requant is therefore expected encoder behaviour, not a port regression. No committed claim quotes an IQ3_S identity rate, so nothing recomputes wrong. Recorded here so the next sweep reads it as a number, not as a surprise."
  ]
